== Close

#smallcaps[If] my reader has not followed me step by step as he has read my pages, I am truly sorry. Reading books is of little value unless the truths which pass before the mind are grasped, made one’s own, and carried out in practice. It is as if someone saw plenty of food in a shop and yet stayed hungry, for lack of eating any of it himself. It is all in vain, dear reader, that you and I have met, unless you have actually taken hold of Christ Jesus, my Lord. On my part there was a clear desire to do you good, and I have done my best to that end. It pains me that I have not been able to do you good, for I have longed to win that privilege. I was thinking of you when I wrote this page, and I laid down my pen and solemnly knelt in prayer for everyone who would read it. It is my firm conviction that great numbers of readers will receive a blessing, even though #emph[you] refuse to be one of them. But why should #emph[you] refuse? If you do not desire the choice blessing which I wanted to bring you, at least do me the justice of admitting that the blame for your final doom will not lie at my door. #emph[When we two meet before the great white throne, you will not be able to charge me with having idly used the attention which you were kind enough to give me while you were reading my little book]. God knows I wrote each line for your eternal good. I now in spirit take you by the hand. I give you a firm grip. Do you feel my brotherly grasp? The tears are in my eyes as I look at you and say, #emph[Why will you die]? Will you not give your soul a thought? Will you perish through sheer carelessness? Oh, do not do so; but weigh these solemn matters, and make sure of eternity. Do not refuse Jesus, his love, his blood, his salvation. Why should you do so? Can you do it?

#align(center)[I #smallcaps[beg you],]

#align(center)[#smallcaps[Do not turn away from your Redeemer]!]

If, on the other hand, my prayers are heard, and you, my reader, have been led to trust the Lord Jesus and receive salvation by grace from him, then hold always to this doctrine, and this way of living. Let Jesus be your all in all, and let free grace be the one line in which you live and move. There is no life like that of one who lives in the favor of God. To receive everything as a free gift keeps the mind from self-righteous pride, and from self-accusing despair. It makes the heart grow warm with grateful love, and so it creates a feeling in the soul which is infinitely more acceptable to God than anything that can possibly come from slavish fear. Those who hope to be saved by trying to do their best know nothing of that glowing fervor, that holy warmth, that devout joy in God, which come with salvation freely given according to the grace of God. The slavish spirit of self-salvation is no match for the joyous spirit of adoption. There is more real worth in the slightest stirring of faith than in all the tugging of bond-slaves to the law, or all the weary machinery of devotees who would climb to heaven by rounds of ceremonies. Faith is spiritual, and God, who is a spirit, delights in it for that reason. Years of saying prayers, and church-going or chapel-going, and ceremonies, and performances, may be only an abomination in the sight of the spiritual Jehovah; but a glance from the eye of true faith is spiritual, and so it is dear to him. “The Father is seeking such as these to worship Him.” Look first to the inner man, and to the spiritual part of religion, and the rest will then follow in due course.

#emph[If you are saved yourself, be on the watch for the souls of others]. Your own heart will not prosper unless it is filled with intense concern to bless your fellow men. The life of your soul lies in faith; its health lies in love. He who does not long to lead others to Jesus has never been under the spell of love himself. Get to the work of the Lord — the work of love. Begin at home. Visit your neighbors next. Bring light to the village, or the street where you live. Scatter the word of the Lord wherever your hand can reach.

If those who are converted become winners of others, who knows what may spring from my little book? Already I begin praising God for the conversions which he will work by it, and by those whom it leads to Jesus. Probably most of the results will come when my right hand, which is now leaving its mark on the page, lies paralyzed in death.

#smallcaps[Reader], #smallcaps[meet me in heaven]! #emph[Do not go down to hell]. There is no coming back from that place of misery. Why do you want to enter the way of death when heaven’s gate is open before you? Do not refuse the free pardon, the full salvation which Jesus grants to all who trust him. Do not hesitate and delay. You have had enough of resolving; come to action. Believe in Jesus now, with full and immediate decision. Take words with you and come to your Lord today, this very day. Remember, O soul, it may be

#align(center)[#smallcaps[now or never]]

with you. Let it be #smallcaps[now]\; it would be horrible if it were #emph[never].

Farewell. Again I charge you,

#align(center)[#smallcaps[meet me in heaven].]
